  <script>window.__RM_ALLOW_PHASE2_POOLING = true;</script>
  <script>window.__verdict = {"verdict":"OLD"}; window.__quarantinedTrials = {"OLD":{}};</script>
  <div id="rapidmeta-integrity-badge"></div>
  ```
  Consequence: the regex replaces only the phase-2 script, leaves the later old verdict script in place, and the browser can end with `window.__verdict === OLD`.

- **SELECTOR KEYED TO HTML-LIKE TEXT, NOT HTML STRUCTURE**: line 367, same defect repeated at line 499.  
  Exact badge input:
  ```html
  <div id="rapidmeta-integrity-badge"><script>const x="</div>";</script><b>old</b></div>
  ```
  Consequence: the scanner treats `"</div>"` inside JavaScript as the real closing tag and leaves a malformed tail after replacement.

- **VALUES CHANGED BY LINE-ENDING NORMALISATION**: lines 342/484 and 491/541.  
  Exact input: valid `APIXABAN_ACS_AUTO_FULL_REVIEW.html` and `APIXABAN_ACS_AUTO_REVIEW.html` stored with CRLF (`\r\n`) line endings.  
  Consequence: Python reads with universal newlines and writes with `newline=""`, so unchanged surviving content is rewritten as LF-only and byte/text gates can report false changes.

- **INSTRUMENT READING A DIFFERENT COPY / NO COPY**: line 57 names `LEDGER`, but lines 244 and 317 hardcode the ledger values.  
  Exact input:
  ```json
  {"NCT00831441":{"previous_ledger_values":{"tE":516,"tN":3687,"cE":489,"cN":3705}}}
  ```
  Consequence: the output still reports `515/489` and `284/413`, so ledger drift is invisible.

No finding: check-cannot-fail, probe keyed to removed string, idempotency guard satisfied by own comment, merged-cell/off-by-one tabulation, zero conflated with absent, negation dropped, status-code wrapper.
